{
  "version": "virtuals-v3",
  "namespace": "virtuals",
  "description": "Retrieval-verification dataset for the virtuals namespace: read-only agent-token screening, single-agent detail, the graduation feed, the genesis sale calendar, the bonding-curve trade tape, pool price candles, the agent creator's trading-fee status (including the measured refusal of a claim), (PR-C2) the two bonding-curve TRADE tools, and (PR-C3) the four bonding-curve LAUNCH tools. Blind rows describe the outcome without naming the brand; protocol-aware rows name it. The trade rows deliberately separate PRICING from SIGNING: an agent that asks what something would cost must reach the quote, and one that says buy must reach the execute, so a row that reaches the wrong half is a retrieval defect and not a near miss. The launch rows separate the four states an agent launch can be in - pricing it, signing it, observing whether the keeper has run, and cancelling one that never went live - for the same reason and with more at stake: a row that wanted a price and reached the execute would spend, and one that wanted the state and reached the cancel would undo a launch that is still pending.",
